# Trivy vulnerability exceptions.
#
# Empty by default - every CRITICAL/HIGH finding currently fails the build
# (see .github/workflows/pipeline.yaml, "security-scan" job).
#
# If a finding is a false positive, or is genuinely unfixable/not
# exploitable in our deployment (e.g. no network path to the vulnerable
# code), add the CVE ID here with a comment explaining why and, ideally, an
# expiry/review date so exceptions don't accumulate silently:
#
# CVE-2024-XXXXX  # not exploitable: vulnerable code path is unreachable, we don't use <feature>. Review by 2026-12-01.
#
# In a real production setting this would live in a vulnerability
# management tool (e.g. Dependency-Track) instead of a flat file, so
# exceptions have owners, expiry dates, and an audit trail. See the
# top-level README "Missing improvements" section.
